# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Crow — Garage secrets (the root docker-compose.yml `garage` service only)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#   cp .env.garage.example .env.garage    # then fill in the five values below
#
# `.env.garage` is what the `garage` service reads (`env_file:` in the root compose),
# and nothing else reads it. It is gitignored — never commit it.
#
# Why a file of its own: the gateway loads `.env`, and Garage's admin token, RPC secret
# and metrics token must never reach the gateway process. The gateway reaches Garage
# over S3 with one key pair only — S3_ACCESS_KEY / S3_SECRET_KEY in `.env` — so the two
# files share just that pair, copied by hand. This is the same rule the File Storage
# (Garage) extension follows: it writes S3_ACCESS_KEY / S3_SECRET_KEY into the gateway's
# `.env` and keeps GARAGE_ADMIN_TOKEN / GARAGE_RPC_SECRET / GARAGE_METRICS_TOKEN in its
# own settings (tests/garage-bundle.test.js, "the gateway gets S3_* only").
#
# Generate each value and paste the resulting LINE here — Compose does not expand
# $(…) inside an env file, so the values have to be literal in this file.

# Internal RPC secret between Garage's own processes. 64 hex characters. Garage
# refuses to start without it. Never needed outside the garage container.
#   echo "GARAGE_RPC_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32)"
GARAGE_RPC_SECRET=

# Full-control token for Garage's admin API on 127.0.0.1:3903. Any long random string.
# It is the cluster admin credential: it stays in this file, never in `.env`.
#   echo "GARAGE_ADMIN_TOKEN=$(openssl rand -hex 32)"
GARAGE_ADMIN_TOKEN=

# Token for Garage's metrics endpoint. Any long random string.
#   echo "GARAGE_METRICS_TOKEN=$(openssl rand -hex 32)"
GARAGE_METRICS_TOKEN=

# The S3 key pair the gateway uses. Garage creates this key on its first start
# (--default-access-key) and refuses to start if its secret changes, so keep both
# values. COPY BOTH into `.env` as S3_ACCESS_KEY / S3_SECRET_KEY — same pair, both
# sides, or the gateway cannot read a single object.
#
# Key ID: "GK" + 24 hex characters.
#   echo "GARAGE_DEFAULT_ACCESS_KEY=GK$(openssl rand -hex 12)"    # -> also .env S3_ACCESS_KEY
GARAGE_DEFAULT_ACCESS_KEY=

# Secret half of that S3 key pair: 64 hex characters.
#   echo "GARAGE_DEFAULT_SECRET_KEY=$(openssl rand -hex 32)"      # -> also .env S3_SECRET_KEY
GARAGE_DEFAULT_SECRET_KEY=